  "title": "Hold that bit",
  "format": "build",
  "skills": [
    "logic.d-latch",
    "logic.memory"
  ],
  "brief": {
    "story": "The SR latch remembered, but needed two buttons. A D latch has one data switch (D) and a STORE button (E): while STORE is held, Q copies D; let go and Q keeps that value, whatever D does next. Four NANDs and an inverter. The feedback that makes it remember is missing.",
    "goal": "Wire the two feedback links so Q copies D while STORE is held, and holds it after.",
    "datasheet": {
      "title": "Gated D latch",
      "rows": [
        [
          "IC1 74HC04",
          "NOT D → column 4"
        ],
        [
          "IC2 gates 1, 2",
          "S̄ = NAND(D, E) · R̄ = NAND(NOT D, E)"
        ],
        [
          "IC2 gates 3, 4",
          "Q = NAND(S̄, Q̄) · Q̄ = NAND(R̄, Q)"
        ],
        [
          "Feedback",
          "Q (col 20, bottom) → pin 13 (col 15) · Q̄ (col 17) → pin 10 (col 18)"
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "hints": [
    "Gates 3 and 4 are the SR latch from World 1’s level 9: each one’s output feeds the other one’s input.",
    "Q is pin 8 (column 20, bottom half); it goes to pin 13 (column 15, bottom). Q̄ is pin 11 (column 17, bottom); it goes to pin 10 (column 18, bottom).",
    "Wires: column 20 bottom → column 15 bottom, and column 17 bottom → column 18 bottom."
  ],
